# install-extra.pkgs -- extra packages for the offline install mirror only.
#
# Names listed here are resolved into build/forky-mirror (build-forky-mirror.sh)
# and checked by verify-offline-mirror-seeds.sh, but are NOT installed into
# base.squashfs or desktop.squashfs; a post-install hook installs them.
# One package name per line. Leave empty for images that ship nothing extra.
#
# ncz-screensavers is added here when its .deb is staged in
# build/ncz-screensavers-out/ (see build/build-image.sh). It is now
# MANDATORY on desktop variants (operator 2026-10-05: "If we are
# distributing screensavers as Deb they need to be apt installed during
# installation.") and the offline mirror MUST carry it at the version
# floor in build/screensavers-version.env; build/build-desktop-mirror.sh
# enforces that on pool rebuild and build/build-squashfs-layers.sh +
# build/build-role-delta-mkosi.sh pre-flight it via build/assert-mirror-
# has-screensavers.sh. A mirror that lacks this package will not build.
#
# ncz-screensavers-plugin is intentionally NOT listed: it is not published to
# the NCZ apt repo and it is ABI-coupled to the Singularity payload, so the
# image carries a pinned deb on the install medium and hook 59 installs it
# (post-install/lib/ncz-screensavers-plugin.lock).
ncz-screensavers
#
# ncz-apt-policy (r201 apt separation): the pin that keeps NCZ-OS packages and Debian
# packages apart. Hook 24 writes the pin itself on a fresh install; this package keeps it
# current afterwards (ncz-update-apply installs it on running systems). It must be PUBLISHED
# (>= 1.0.1) before an image or mirror is built.
ncz-apt-policy
#
# The installer's user-setup step runs `apt-get install sudo` in the target, and
# finish-install / pkgsel reach for installation-report and popularity-contest.
# The media's /cdrom index only lists what the seed closure resolved, so on the raw
# GPT images these were "Unable to locate package" / "Package 'sudo' has no
# installation candidate" (user-setup then failed and the first user had no sudo).
sudo
installation-report
popularity-contest
